## 4. Change Orders

No change to the Scope of Work or the Contract Price shall be binding
unless documented in a written Change Order signed by both Parties.
Change Orders shall describe the change, the resulting price delta,
and any schedule impact.

---

## 5. Permits and Inspections

Contractor shall obtain, at Contractor's cost unless itemized as a
reimbursable above, the following permits from the City of
{{ jurisdiction_city }}: building permit, electrical permit, plumbing
permit, and pool barrier permit. Buyer shall cooperate with required
inspections and provide site access.

---

## 6. Liens and Lien Waivers

Upon each milestone payment, Contractor shall deliver a conditional
lien waiver for the amount paid, in a form compliant with Texas
Property Code §53.281 et seq. A final, unconditional lien waiver shall
be delivered upon final payment. Contractor represents that all
subcontractors and suppliers shall be paid from funds received.

---

## 7. Warranty

Contractor warrants the Work against defects in materials and
workmanship for **{{ quote.warranty_years }} year(s)** from the date of
Substantial Completion. Manufacturer warranties for equipment pass
through to Buyer. This warranty excludes damage caused by misuse,
freezing without proper winterization, ground movement not caused by
Contractor's workmanship, and third-party alterations.

---

## 8. Pool Barrier / Safety Compliance

Buyer acknowledges that Texas Health & Safety Code §757 and the City of
{{ jurisdiction_city }} pool barrier ordinances require a compliant
enclosure, self-closing and self-latching gates, and (where applicable)
an alarm on doors leading from the residence to the pool area. Unless
expressly included in Section 1.2, fence and barrier construction is
the responsibility of Buyer and must be inspected and approved prior to
filling the pool.

---

## 9. Insurance

Contractor shall maintain commercial general liability insurance with
minimum limits of $1,000,000 per occurrence / $2,000,000 aggregate and
shall provide a certificate of insurance naming Buyer as additional
insured upon request. Contractor shall also maintain workers'
compensation insurance as required by Texas law.

---

## 10. Dispute Resolution

The Parties shall first attempt in good faith to resolve any dispute
arising out of this Agreement through direct negotiation. If
unresolved within thirty (30) days, the dispute shall be submitted to
non-binding mediation in Collin County, Texas, before a mediator
mutually agreed by the Parties. Any unresolved dispute thereafter
shall be brought exclusively in the state or federal courts located in
Collin County, Texas. Texas law governs this Agreement.

---

